From: Aurelia contributors
Subject: Fix VLC core buffer sizes, FIFO access and current toolchain diagnostics

Keep borrowed input pointers const, allocate terminators for C-string lookup tables,
use the locked FIFO byte-count API, and use the integer type for plugin-cache alignment.
Retry interruption channel I/O on EINTR, accept an already pending nonblocking wake,
and handle unexpected channel failures rather than dropping the result. Preserve the
VLC 3 display callback ABI in an anonymous union while keeping its public deprecated
name annotated; core dispatch uses the explicitly named legacy compatibility slot.

--- a/include/vlc_vout_display.h
+++ b/include/vlc_vout_display.h
@@ -330,7 +330,12 @@
     int        (*control)(vout_display_t *, int, va_list);
 
     /* Manage pending event (optional) */
-    void       (*manage)(vout_display_t *) VLC_DEPRECATED;
+    union {
+        void   (*manage)(vout_display_t *) VLC_DEPRECATED;
+        /* Same ABI slot: core must still dispatch callbacks from VLC 3 modules,
+         * while new modules remain warned against the deprecated public name. */
+        void   (*manage_legacy)(vout_display_t *);
+    };
 
